---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Medical Disclaimer | Real BMI"
    description="Review the official Real BMI medical disclaimer. Our calculators offer educational health estimates based on WHO & CDC references and are not diagnostic tools."
    canonicalURL="https://realbmicalculator.com/en/disclaimer/"
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Medical Disclaimer"
      eyebrow="Important health notice"
      description="Understand how Real BMI provides educational health estimates and why you should consult a qualified professional for medical decisions."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
      <div class="max-w-5xl space-y-8 text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed text-base font-normal">
        
        <!-- Summary Callout -->
        <div class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-[var(--card)]/60 border border-[var(--border)]/60">
          <p class="text-base sm:text-lg text-[var(--foreground)] leading-relaxed font-medium">
            The health calculators, reference charts, and educational articles on <strong>Real BMI</strong> are provided strictly for informational awareness and personal wellness tracking. They are designed to help you understand public health benchmarks at home, but they do not constitute medical advice or clinical diagnosis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 1. Educational Scope & Non-Diagnostic Notice -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            1. Educational Scope &amp; Non-Diagnostic Nature
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI offers computational health tools calibrated directly to published literature from the World Health Organization (WHO), Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), and peer-reviewed journals. What our platform provides:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Mathematical Estimations:</strong> Directional metrics (such as BMI, BMR, TDEE, and body composition) derived from established clinical equations.</li>
            <li><strong>Reference Benchmarks:</strong> Standard statistical cutoffs to help contextualize your numbers against general population guidelines.</li>
            <li><strong>Self-Directed Awareness:</strong> Educational information intended to help you formulate informed questions for your healthcare provider.</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="pt-1">
            <strong>What Real BMI does not provide:</strong> We do not operate a clinic, medical practice, or healthcare advisory board. Output values are never medical diagnoses, individualized clinical evaluations, or therapeutic prescriptions. Never alter medication doses or initiate drastic lifestyle changes based solely on automated calculation results.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 2. Emergency Situations (Callout Box) -->
        <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/5 border border-amber-500/20 text-[var(--foreground)] space-y-2">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
            </svg>
            2. Emergency Medical Assistance
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Immediate Care for Urgent Symptoms
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)]">
            Real BMI is not designed or equipped for medical emergencies. If you or someone with you experiences chest pressure, shortness of breath, sudden numbness, severe dizziness, heart palpitations, or any life-threatening symptoms, immediately call your local emergency service (911 in the United States and Canada, 112 in Europe and India, 999 in the United Kingdom) or go to the nearest emergency room.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. When to Consult a Qualified Doctor or Dietitian -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            3. When to Consult a Healthcare Professional
          </h2>
          <p>
            We strongly urge you to consult a licensed physician, clinical dietitian, or certified health professional before taking action, especially if you:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li>Plan to undertake significant weight loss, rapid weight gain, or restrictive dietary regimens.</li>
            <li>Manage chronic medical conditions such as type 2 diabetes, cardiovascular disease, hypertension, kidney disorders, or thyroid imbalances.</li>
            <li>Take prescription medications whose therapeutic dosage correlates with body mass or metabolic rate (e.g., insulin, antihypertensives).</li>
            <li>Are pregnant, planning pregnancy, breastfeeding, or recovering from surgery.</li>
            <li>Have a personal history of eating disorders, disordered eating patterns, or severe body image distress.</li>
            <li>Notice unexplained, rapid fluctuations in your body weight or persistent fluid retention.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 4. Scientific & Physiological Limitations of Screening Tools -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            4. Scientific &amp; Physiological Limitations
          </h2>
          <p>
            Standard anthropometric screening tools possess inherent physiological limitations that must be considered when reviewing results:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2">
            <li><strong>Body Composition vs. Total Mass:</strong> BMI calculates the mass-to-height ratio (kg/m²). It cannot differentiate between dense skeletal muscle, bone mineral density, and adipose tissue. Muscular athletes frequently classify as "overweight" or "obese" despite having very low body fat percentages.</li>
            <li><strong>Age-Related Sarcopenia:</strong> In adults aged 65 and older, natural muscle wasting (sarcopenia) can mask significant abdominal adiposity behind a seemingly "normal" BMI score. Geriatric clinical literature often identifies a slightly higher BMI (23.0 to 27.9 kg/m²) as protective against bone fractures and frailty.</li>
            <li><strong>Ethnic Cardiometabolic Differences:</strong> Adiposity distribution varies significantly by ancestry. The WHO recognizes that adults of Asian and South Asian heritage face heightened risks of insulin resistance and cardiovascular disease at lower thresholds, recommending an overweight cutoff of 23.0 kg/m² instead of 25.0 kg/m².</li>
            <li><strong>Pediatric &amp; Adolescent Growth:</strong> Adult BMI formulas must never be applied to individuals under 18. Growing children must be evaluated using age- and sex-specific growth percentiles (CDC/WHO growth charts) interpreted by a pediatrician.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <!-- 5. Risks of Severe Caloric Restriction & Medication Adjustments -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            5. Risks of Unsupervised Caloric Deficits &amp; Medication Changes
          </h2>
          <p>
            Never alter, titrate, or discontinue prescription medications based on metrics obtained from our tools. Changes in body composition and weight alter pharmacokinetics and drug clearance; dosage adjustments must be supervised by your prescribing physician.
          </p>
          <p>
            Additionally, adopting severe caloric restrictions (such as consuming fewer than 1,200 kcal/day for women or 1,500 kcal/day for men) without clinical oversight carries substantial health risks, including metabolic adaptation, electrolyte imbalances, gallstone development, nutrient deficiencies, and lean tissue loss. Always seek clinical guidance before implementing major nutritional adjustments.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 6. Directional Proxies vs. Diagnostic Laboratory Biomarkers -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            6. Screening Proxies vs. Comprehensive Laboratory Diagnostics
          </h2>
          <p>
            Anthropometric indices (such as BMI, waist-to-hip ratio, and body fat estimates) are preliminary screening proxies. While they provide useful population-level correlations, they do not replace comprehensive clinical health evaluations.
          </p>
          <p>
            Authentic cardiometabolic assessment requires direct diagnostic biomarkers: fasting plasma glucose, HbA1c, comprehensive lipid panels (total cholesterol, HDL, LDL, triglycerides), and resting blood pressure measurements conducted in a clinical setting. Use our tools to prepare informed, constructive questions for your routine healthcare checkups.
          </p>
        </section>

        <!-- 7. Limitation of Liability & Independent Governance -->
        <section class="space-y-3">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            7. Limitation of Liability &amp; Independent Governance
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is an independent software engineering initiative created and maintained by <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> (Banswara, Rajasthan, India). All calculation models are implemented directly from published WHO, CDC, and ICMR standards. The platform does not operate a multidisciplinary medical board, hospital affiliation, or physician review committee.
          </p>
          <p>
            To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, Real BMI and its creators disclaim all liability for any personal health decisions, dietary adjustments, physical training regimens, or health outcomes resulting from the use of information or calculations on this website. You utilize these computational tools voluntarily and at your sole discretion. For questions regarding our mathematical models or research citations, please visit our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline font-medium hover:text-[var(--foreground)] transition-colors">Contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
